{{! "Preview" is this step's own word, so it gets defined before it's used -
    the answer means nothing to someone who doesn't know what arrives.

    The card hangs off this line rather than a line below the chips, because
    this one doesn't change with the selection - someone about to pick nobody is
    exactly who benefits from seeing what they'd be sending. }}
<p class="gh-publish-step-note" data-test-text="preview-explainer">
    A preview is everything above your email
    <Editor::Modals::PublishFlow::PaywallHint @preview={{this.paywallPreview}} @below={{true}} />
</p>

{{! No yes/no in front of this: picking someone is the yes, and clearing the
    selection is the no. The other steps all answer their question with one
    control, and a preview sent to nobody is just a preview that isn't sent.

    Everyone the full send already reaches is hidden, so a member can't be sent
    both the post and the teaser for it. }}
<GhMembersRecipientSelect
    @filter={{@publishOptions.previewFilter}}
    @newsletter={{@publishOptions.newsletter}}
    @onChange={{@publishOptions.setPreviewFilter}}
    @hideSegments={{this.hiddenSegments}}
    @renderInPlace={{false}}
    @dropdownClass="gh-publish-newsletter-dropdown"
/>

{{! Only the empty answer gets said out loud. A selection speaks for itself -
    the chips name it and carry its count, the question above asked for it, and
    the review confirms it again at the end. Restating it here was the same
    sentence twice on one screen. Nobody is the one answer that would otherwise
    read as a step left unfinished. }}
{{#unless this.previewSummary}}
    <p class="gh-publish-step-callout" data-test-step-access>No preview will be sent.</p>
{{/unless}}
